{#
  supplementary-block.njk — mode-aware auxiliary content blocks.
  Each mode carries one supplementary block with a heading, kind tag,
  and markdown content. The block is optional per profile; this partial
  silently skips modes that have no supplementaryByMode entry.

  Required in scope: profile.supplementaryByMode

  Content rendering: block.contentMarkdown is rendered via the `markdown`
  filter (added to eleventy.config.js as part of WM-1B). Filter converts
  markdown-it-rendered HTML; use `| safe` to output without escaping.
  markdown-it config: html: true (allows table markup in neutral-mode
  data block), linkify: false.

  Note on TBD links in supplementary markdown: some contentMarkdown fields
  (gapView) contain links with href="TBD" that will render as <a href="TBD">.
  These are placeholder links from the M2 prototype. The CTA TBD check applies
  to cta-block.njk only; markdown content TBD links are left as-is for v1.
  Flag: admin to decide whether to post-process or hand-write around TBD
  links in supplementaryByMode markdown (PUBLIC_CONTENT M4 or later).

  Mobile behavior: <details>/<summary> handles expand-on-click natively with
  no JS. CSS forces the content visible on desktop regardless of open state.
  On mobile (≤768px), browser manages show/hide via the details element.

  Kind tag values and their CSS modifiers:
    summary → .supplementary-block--summary
    action  → .supplementary-block--action
    reform  → .supplementary-block--reform
    data    → .supplementary-block--data
#}

{%- set supp = profile.supplementaryByMode -%}
{#- Synthesis #}
{%- if supp.synthesis %}
<div class="mode-content" data-mode-show="synthesis">
  <section class="supplementary-block supplementary-block--{{ supp.synthesis.kind }}">
    <details>
      <summary class="supplementary-block__heading">
        {{ supp.synthesis.title }}
        <span class="supplementary-block__kind-tag">{{ supp.synthesis.kind }}</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="supplementary-block__content">
        {{ supp.synthesis.contentMarkdown | markdown | safe }}
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
</div>
{%- endif %}
{#- Design view #}
{%- if supp.designView %}
<div class="mode-content" data-mode-show="design">
  <section class="supplementary-block supplementary-block--{{ supp.designView.kind }}">
    <details>
